course: dictionary
lesson: 8723
title: Apart, one at a time
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Separately is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done. It means apart, not together, or one at a time, each on its own. «Wash the dark clothes and the white clothes separately» means do not put them in the same wash.
explain: Use the context to check. «Work out each part separately, then add them.» The word each and the word then tell you to do one part first, then the next. Swap in your meaning, one at a time, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Words can be sorted into types. Separately is not a thing you can hold, like a sock or a spoon. It describes an action, such as washing, testing or marking. «Her family washes knives separately and puts them away at once» tells you how they wash them: on their own, away from other things.
fact: Separately means apart, not together.
fact: Separately often means one at a time, or each on its own.
fact: Separately is an adverb, because it tells you how something is done.
fact: In science, you test each material separately, because a fair test changes one thing at a time.
fact: «Evolved the same trick separately» means the sugar glider and the flying squirrel each developed the trick on their own, not together.
exercise: «Wash the dark clothes and the white clothes separately.» What does separately mean here? | Quickly and loudly | *Apart, one load at a time | Very dirty | Together in one big load
exercise: «Sort the glass, the paper and the plastic separately.» Which idea does separately give? | Very fast | *Each kind on its own | All in one pile | Anywhere at all
exercise: Find the word in «Work out each part separately, then add them.» that tells you how to do the work. | each | add | *separately | work
test: Ella says separately means together. Why is she wrong? | Separately means very loud | Separately is a noun for a school bag | Separately means together, always | *Separately means apart, not together
test: «Many scientists think they grew quills separately.» What does separately suggest? | *They grew quills on their own, not copied from each other | They grew quills in the same way, together | They grew quills by accident in a shop | They grew quills in the sea
exam: Which meaning fits best? «The two are marked separately.» | Neither is marked at all | *Each one gets its own mark | Both are marked very quickly | Both are marked with one shared mark
